      "excerpt": "63685 - Insertion or replacement of spinal neurostimulator pulse generator or receiver, direct or inductive coupling, with connection to electrode array\nCPT 63650 (percutaneous implantation of neurostimulator electrode array, epidural) and CPT 63685 (insertion of a permanent spinal neurostimulator pulse generator/receiver) describe fundamentally different encounters and are not interchangeable. A percutaneous SCS trial - leads placed and externalized to a temporary trial stimulator for a defined home trial period, with no generator pocketed or implanted - maps to 63650, regardless of whether the leads are later removed or the patient proceeds to a permanent system at a separate future encounter. 63685 requires that an implantable pulse generator actually be opened, prepared, and connected to the electrode array during the encounter being billed. Reviewers should confirm the presence (or explicit absence) of a permanent generator serial/model number and pocket-creation documentation before accepting either code."
